# Silences Node's DEP0040 punycode deprecation warning on every `npm run` in this repo.
#
# The bare `require("punycode")` behind it is not ours and not fixable from here — it
# lives in vendored/transitive code:
#   next/dist/compiled/node-fetch/index.js   (Next.js's own bundled copy)
#   node-fetch/node_modules/{tr46,whatwg-url}
# Nothing we declare pulls it in directly, so there is no version to bump; it is pure
# noise on every dev request.
#
# Scoped to this one warning rather than a blanket --no-deprecation, so real
# deprecation warnings still get through. Must live at the repo root: npm ignores
# .npmrc inside a workspace package ("ignoring workspace config").
node-options=--disable-warning=DEP0040
